==German==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|de|deyḱ}}
Old High German ''zēha'' from an original *''tēha'', compare Dutch [[teen]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtseːə/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Zehe.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|Zehe|Zehen}}

# [[clove]] {{gloss|of garlic and similar plants}}
# {{lb|de|regional}} [[toe]]

====Usage notes====
''Zehe'' as meaning “toe” is universally understood, but rare in most regions. The form is common in {{l|de|Saxony}} (and bordering parts of East Central Germany) as well as parts of {{l|de|Austria}}.<ref>http://www.atlas-alltagssprache.de/genus/</ref> The more widespread form is {{m|de|Zeh}} (of masculine gender).
